{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>כאשר.</b> The commentators said that כאשר is like כעוצם, and this is futile, for its meaning is the body of the offspring before it is born. And see עצמים, for they are the foundations of the body, for the flesh and skin are like a garment. And המלאה is pregnancy, and it is possible that המלאה is an adjective for the woman, and the word בטן is in construct state. And also it is possible for it to be an adjective for בטן, for to all of them it is feminine in the sacred language. And the first bet ought to be open and the second dagesh, and like it לאיש העשיר."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra disputes commentators who read כאשר כעצמים as 'like the bones'; the bet/dagesh remark concerns whether each bet in the phrase is lenited or fortified, tied to the construct-state question."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:09.762627787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}